      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_b07da806",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: the_holocaust_is_a_sad_moment_in_history; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts Adolf Hitler, a central figure in the Holocaust, with the text 'the holocaust is a sad moment in history.' This juxtaposition trivializes the Holocaust — a genocide that resulted in the systematic murder of six million Jews and millions of others — by reducing it to a mere 'sad moment.' This minimization is a form of Holocaust denial or minimization, which is a harmful and dangerous trope that distorts historical truth, undermines the suffering of victims, and can embolden hate. The intent is to mock or dismiss the gravity of the Holocaust, thereby normalizing or trivializing genocide, which can have real-world consequences by fostering ignorance and indifference toward atrocities. The meme uses the visual of Hitler to anchor the text in a context of historical horror, making the minimization more shocking and provocative.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_8ddcbdae"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
